---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---

<div class="title-row" style="display: flex; align-items: left; gap: 5%;">
  <img src="/assets/images/me.png" alt="Photo of {{ site.name }}" class="home-photo"/>
  <hgroup class="title-card">
    <h1>{{ site.name }}</h1>
    <h5>{{ site.title }}</h5>
    <h5>{{ site.institution }}</h5>
    <div style="margin-top: 0.25rem;"></div>
    <h6>
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
    </h6>
    <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"></div>
    <h6>
      {{ site.office.room }}<br>
      {{ site.office.street }}<br>
      {{ site.office.city }}
    </h6>
  </hgroup>
</div>

<br>

<article>
  <p>
    I am a computer science PhD candidate at
    <a href="https://www.northwestern.edu/" target="_blank">Northwestern University</a>
    in Evanston, Illinois. I currently work in the {{ site.lab }} with Dr. Peter Dinda.
  </p>
  <p>
    My research interests primarily lie in architecture-aware optimizations for parallel systems,
    with work ranging from synchronization primitives to wimpy-node/efficient computing clusters.
    My recent focus has been on low-level performance engineering for database execution engines
    (vectorized and compilation based).
  </p>
  <p>
    I earned my bachelor's degree in electrical &amp; computer engineering from
    <a href="https://www.olin.edu" target="_blank">Olin College of Engineering</a>,
    focusing on work in power electronics, software systems, and hardware design (ASICs to PCBs).
  </p>
  <p>
    From 2021&ndash;2025, I interned working on the IBM Z mainframes as a part of the Millicode and
    System Architecture teams. Most recently I worked on formalizing the z/Architecture memory model
    from its specifications.
  </p>
</article>

<article>
  <h2>News</h2>

  <hr />

  <dl class="news-list">
    {% for item in news | sort("date") | reverse %}
    <dt><time datetime="{{ item.date }}">{{ item.date | dateFormat("MMM yyyy") }}</time></dt>
    <dd>{{ item.text }}</dd>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
</article>

